4.vi
    Recall that rinf(c) in a steady state solution for a long enough time
    rinf(c) = 8.0*10^4*C^(-0.602)

    theirfore Rs(0) = Rinf(5) = 30361 ohms
    The concentration jumps to 50 ppm at \(t=0\) and remains there. The sensor
    resistance gradually approaches Rinf2 = Rinf(50) = 7591.2 Ohm

    Theirfore,
    22r'(t) + r(t) = 7591.2 with initial condition r(0) = 30361
    Solving this differential we using the same method as before we get
    r'(t) + 1/22 * r(t) = 7591.2/22

    u(x) = e^(integral(1/22)dt) => e^t/22

    r(t) * e^t/22 - 30361 = 7591.2/22 * integral(e^t/22) [ 0, t]
    r(t) *  e^t/22 = 7591.2/22 * integral(e^t/22) [ 0, t] + 30361
    r(t) =  e^-t/22 * 7591.2/22 * integral(e^t/22) [ 0, t] + 30361 *  e^-t/22
    r(t) =  (e^-t/22) * 7591.2 * (e^t/22 - 1) + 30361 *  e^-t/22
    r(t) = 7591.2 -7591.2e^-t/22 + 30361e^-t/22
    r(t) = 7591.2 + e^-t/22 * 22769.8

